==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|bidon||small portable container, sealed and made of wood or metal|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|non|fr}} *{{term||bida, *biða|container, vessel|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fr}} {{recons|bidōn|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|bidjan||tub, vessel, vat|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fr}} {{recons|bʰidʰ-||pot, bucket, barrel|lang=ine-pro}}, from {{recons|bʰeydʰ-||to weave, bind|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|biða||milkbucket|lang=is}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|bide||churn|lang=no}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|bidne||vessel|lang=no}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|fidelia|fidēlia|clay or glass vessel|lang=la}}, {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|πίθος||tr=píthos|wine barrel|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-bidon.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|/bi.dɔ̃/|lang=fr}}
* {{rhymes|dɔ̃|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# [[can]], [[tin]], [[canister]]
# (''childish language'') [[tummy]]

===Adjective===
{{fr-adj|inv=yes|type=inv}}

# {{context|slang|lang=fr}} [[rigged]]
#: La course de chevaux est '''bidon'''.
# {{context|slang|lang=fr}} [[phoney]], [[sham]]
#: Ces cris et ces pleurs sont '''bidon''' puisqu'elle ne l'aimait pas.
# {{context|slang|lang=fr}} [[crap]]
#: Ce film est complètement '''bidon'''.

===Derived terms===
* {{l/fr|bidonville}}

===Anagrams===
* [[bondi#French|bondi]]

